   "title": "Newspaper vocabulary added",
   "text": "87,299 of the reference words come from a newspaper corpus (Leipzig Corpora Collection, tel_newscrawl_2011_300K, 4.3 million words); 10,586 come from the subtitle list. Written sources are more formal than subtitles and contain more names and foreign words. Frequencies of the corpus-only words come from that corpus and are not comparable with subtitle frequencies."
  },
  {
   "title": "Abugida: CV and length",
